# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Agentic Operator — environment template
#  Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you actually use.
#  `.env.local` is gitignored — never commit real secrets.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  STEP 0 — Choose your deployment topology FIRST.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  ┌─ Topology A: Solo dev (AO on your laptop) ───────────────────────┐
#  │  AO + Inngest both on YOUR machine. Partner systems are remote.   │
#  │  Bridge events from partner Inngest in/out when you want to       │
#  │  exercise the real pipeline.                                       │
#  │  • Run a local Inngest dev:                                       │
#  │      node_modules/.bin/inngest-cli dev --host 0.0.0.0             │
#  │  • INNGEST_* keep localhost:8288 defaults below                   │
#  │  • Optional §10 (RAAS bridge) only if you want auto-pull          │
#  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
#  ┌─ Topology B: Deploy AO inside partner infrastructure ────────────┐
#  │  AO becomes one of N SDK apps registered with partner's EXISTING  │
#  │  Inngest. ONE Inngest server for everyone — no bridging needed.   │
#  │  • DO NOT run a second inngest-cli — use partner's existing one    │
#  │  • INNGEST_* point to partner's existing Inngest URL/keys         │
#  │  • ⛔ Skip §10 entirely — bridge solves a problem that doesn't     │
#  │    exist in same-Inngest mode (would cause duplicate events)      │
#  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  ARCHITECTURE NOTE — Where AO talks to Neo4j
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  AO does NOT need its own direct Neo4j credentials for normal use.
#  It reads + writes Neo4j entities through Allmeta Studio (§5):
#
#      AO  ──HTTP──→  Allmeta Studio (:3500)  ──bolt──→  Neo4j
#                     (one place owns Neo4j config)
#
#  This means:
#    ✓ rule-check reads rules           → via Allmeta (§5)
#    ✓ chatbot resolves candidate names → via Allmeta (§5)
#    ✓ audit drawer reads candidate JSON → via Allmeta (§5)
#    ✓ writes for Candidate / Resume / JD / Match Result → via Allmeta (§5)
#
#  Only ONE niche feature still uses direct bolt:// to Neo4j:
#  rule-check writing its own audit nodes for graph navigation.
#  Configure §7 only if you want that specific feature; otherwise the
#  Prisma `RuleCheckAudit` table (always written) covers the UI.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                       MUST CONFIGURE                              ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ─── 1. Persistence — AO's own SQLite (zero deploy) ──────────────────
# Stores: WorkflowRun, EventInstance, RuleCheckAudit, AuditLog,
# BehaviorAlert, AgentEpisode, AgentActivity, AgentConfig — all AO's
# operational state. Auto-created on first `npx prisma migrate dev`.
# No DB server to install; single file at the path below.
DATABASE_URL="file:./data/ao.db"


# ─── 2. Agent file-logger output ─────────────────────────────────────
# Per-agent JSON-lines log files land here as <agent>-YYYY-MM-DD.log.
# Captures every Postgres + Neo4j read/write, every handler start/done,
# every event emit. Use an absolute path (relative paths break when the
# dev-server cwd shifts).
AO_LOG_DIR=/absolute/path/to/agenticOperator/logs


# ─── 3. Inngest event bus ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Inngest is the runtime that delivers events to AO's agent functions.
# In Topology A you run a local inngest-cli; in Topology B you use
# partner's existing Inngest. The SDK reads these env vars implicitly
# (no `process.env` ref in our code) — keep all six even if grep is empty.

# Where AO's SDK SENDS events to (inngest.send() POST target).
# Topology A: http://localhost:8288   Topology B: partner's Inngest URL.
INNGEST_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8288

# Same value as INNGEST_BASE_URL, read by a different code path inside
# the SDK. Always equal to INNGEST_BASE_URL in dev mode.
INNGEST_DEV=http://localhost:8288

# Inngest's event-write API key. "dev" works against inngest-cli.
# Topology B: use whatever key partner's Inngest expects.
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=dev

# Inngest's webhook-signing key, verifies that incoming /api/inngest
# calls really came from Inngest. "dev" works locally.
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=dev

# Where Inngest can CALL BACK to AO's SDK to dispatch events.
# Topology A (Inngest + AO same host): http://localhost:3002
# Topology B (AO on a server inside partner network): use AO's
# LAN-reachable URL from Inngest's perspective.
INNGEST_SERVE_HOST=http://localhost:3002

# The route path AO mounts its serve adapter at. Don't change unless
# you renamed app/api/inngest/route.ts.
INNGEST_SERVE_PATH=/api/inngest


# ─── 4. LLM gateway ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers rule-check, tracing chatbot, agent reasoning.
#
# AO's pickGateway (server/llm/gateway.ts) tries two modes in order:
#   ① AI_BASE_URL + AI_API_KEY → route via an OpenAI-compatible proxy
#                                  (e.g. new-api at 10.100.0.70:3010).
#                                  Proxy routes AI_MODEL to the actual
#                                  backend (Gemini / Claude / GPT).
#                                  AI_API_KEY is issued BY THE PROXY
#                                  (not OpenAI), despite the "sk-…"
#                                  format mimicking OpenAI's key.
#   ② OPENAI_API_KEY            → direct OpenAI api.openai.com/v1 +
#                                  fixed model gpt-4o-mini.
#
# Pick ONE. The example URL below is partner-specific — if you don't
# have a proxy, comment out the AI_* trio and uncomment OPENAI_API_KEY.

# Base URL of your OpenAI-compatible proxy. Strip trailing slash.
AI_BASE_URL=http://10.100.0.70:3010/v1

# Bearer token issued by the proxy admin (matches what Workflow Studio
# uses in Action_and_Event_Manager/workflow-studio/server/.env).
AI_API_KEY=sk-replace-with-your-proxy-key

# Model name the proxy understands. Convention varies by proxy install —
# new-api uses "<provider>/<model>" prefix, others use bare names.
# Ask your proxy admin for the catalogue.
AI_MODEL=google/gemini-3-flash-preview

# ── Fallback — only used if AI_* above are unset ──
# Real OpenAI sk-... key. The gateway hard-codes model gpt-4o-mini
# and baseURL https://api.openai.com/v1 in this mode.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-real-openai-key


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                       RECOMMENDED                                 ║
# ║   Without these, the matching feature shows a warn banner /       ║
# ║   degrades to empty state, but AO does NOT crash.                 ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ─── 5. Allmeta Ontology Studio (THE ONLY Neo4j access path) ─────────
# Runs in a separate repo (~/allmetaOntology/apps/studio) on port 3500.
# Studio owns the Neo4j connection internally — AO talks HTTP to Studio.
#
# Used by:
#   - rule-check: fetches rule list (fall back to bundled rules.json
#                  when this is unset → newer rules missing)
#   - chatbot:    resolves candidate / JR / client display names
#                  (unset → entities show as raw IDs like "候选人 bf2fd907")
#   - audit drawer: live snapshot of Candidate / Resume nodes in the
#                  drawer's "图引擎 (Allmeta)" panel
#   - allmeta-writers: writes Candidate / Resume / JD / Match Result
#                  through HTTP API (so AO never needs Neo4j creds)
#
# ALLMETA_API_KEY must match Studio's own .env (Studio issues the token).
ALLMETA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3500
ALLMETA_API_KEY=replace-with-studio-token

# Ontology domain namespace — usually "RAAS-v1" for this project.
ALLMETA_DOMAIN=RAAS-v1


# ─── 6. RoboHire (resume parser + match-resume backend) ──────────────
# Production resume parser. AO calls /parse-resume and /match-resume.
# Without it, resume parsing fails per-call (the rest of the pipeline
# can still be demoed via the Inngest dashboard's "Send event" with
# pre-parsed JSON payloads).

# Base URL of RoboHire's API (production fixed at api.robohire.io).
ROBOHIRE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.robohire.io

# Your RoboHire account API key (rh_xxx).
ROBOHIRE_API_KEY=rh_replace_with_your_key

# Per-request timeout in milliseconds. 120000 (2min) handles big resumes.
ROBOHIRE_TIMEOUT_MS=120000


# ╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                       OPTIONAL                                    ║
# ║   For specific deployment scenarios. Leave commented out for     ║
# ║   solo / isolated dev work — AO runs fully without these.        ║
# ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ─── 7. Direct Neo4j access — rarely needed (see ARCHITECTURE NOTE) ──
# §5 Allmeta already covers 99% of AO's Neo4j needs. Configure §7 ONLY
# when you want the audit drawer's specific "rule-check audit graph"
# feature, which writes audit nodes directly via bolt:// for graph
# navigation. Prisma's RuleCheckAudit table (always written) drives
# the audit list + drawer UI — without §7, you just lose one optional
# panel inside the drawer.
#
# Pick Option A or Option B. Don't set both.
#
# Option A — partner's shared Neo4j (VPN / partner-internal):
# RAAS_LINKS_NEO4J_URI=neo4j://10.100.0.70:7687
# RAAS_LINKS_NEO4J_USER=neo4j
# RAAS_LINKS_NEO4J_PASSWORD=replace-with-shared-password
# RAAS_LINKS_NEO4J_DATABASE=neo4j
#
# Option B — local Neo4j (spin up a container):
#   docker run -d --name ao-neo4j -p 7475:7474 -p 7688:7687 \
#     -e NEO4J_AUTH=neo4j/testpassword123 neo4j:5
# NEO4J_INSTANCE_URI=bolt://localhost:7688
# NEO4J_INSTANCE_USER=neo4j
# NEO4J_INSTANCE_PASSWORD=testpassword123
# NEO4J_INSTANCE_DATABASE=neo4j

# Boot-time EventDefinition sync worker. Polls Neo4j for the canonical
# event-schema catalogue and caches it locally. Off-VPN: leave at 1,
# worker logs per-error and retries; boot does NOT block.
# NEO4J_SYNC_ENABLED=1
# NEO4J_SYNC_INTERVAL_MS=300000


# ─── 8. RAAS partner Postgres (direct dual-write) ────────────────────
# AO writes candidate / job_posting / candidate_match_result rows
# directly to partner's Postgres (2026-05-20 architecture; replaces
# the old RAAS HTTP API write path). See spec:
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-05-20-ao-direct-dual-write-event-flow.md
#
# Topology A: configure when integrating real partner data flow.
# Topology B: usually configure — AO is inside partner's network, so
#             writing direct to their Postgres is the simple path.
# RAAS_POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@192.168.1.104:5432/raas_db

# Fallback employee_id used by matchResume when neither the event
# payload NOR the local cache provides claimer_employee_id. Set to a
# real recruiter who has claimed requirements in RAAS (else /match
# rejects the request as "no claimer attached").
# RAAS_DEFAULT_EMPLOYEE_ID=replace-with-real-recruiter-id


# ─── 9. MinIO (resume binary fetch) ─────────────────────────────────
# Partner Nextcloud webhook uploads resume files into this S3-compatible
# bucket. resume-parser-agent fetches the binary by object_key from
# RESUME_DOWNLOADED.payload. Without it, parse fails per-call (still OK
# for solo dev: send test events with already-parsed JSON payloads).

# MINIO_ENDPOINT=192.168.1.104         # host:ip of the MinIO server
# MINIO_PORT=9000                       # S3 API port (web console is on 9001)
# MINIO_USE_SSL=false                   # true only if MinIO terminates TLS
# MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-access-key
# MINIO_SECRET_KEY=replace-with-secret-key


# ─── 10. RAAS cross-machine Inngest bridge ──────────────────────────
#
#  ⛔ TOPOLOGY A ONLY — do NOT configure in Topology B.
#  In Topology B you have ONE Inngest; all AO + RAAS agents register
#  with the same server and events flow directly. Setting these in B
#  causes duplicate event delivery.
#
#  In Topology A: AO has its own local Inngest, partner's Inngest is
#  remote. The bridge pulls RESUME_DOWNLOADED inbound and forwards
#  AO's MATCH_* outbound so the cross-machine pipeline works.

# Partner's Inngest REST URL (the bridge polls /v1/events here).
# RAAS_INNGEST_URL=http://10.100.0.70:8288

# Toggle the inbound bridge worker. 1 = start polling partner Inngest.
# RAAS_BRIDGE_ENABLED=0

# Comma-separated list of event names the bridge mirrors INTO AO.
# RAAS_BRIDGE_EVENTS=RESUME_DOWNLOADED

# How often (ms) the bridge polls partner Inngest. 5000ms = 5s.
# RAAS_BRIDGE_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=5000

# Toggle outbound forwarding. 1 = POST AO's MATCH_* back to partner.
# RAAS_FORWARD_ENABLED=0


# ─── 11. Legacy P3 sidecars (WS / EM as separate services) ──────────
# The current architecture runs WS / EM in-process inside the Next app.
# Keep these commented out unless you have an explicit reason to run
# the old sidecar processes from the P3 migration era.
# WS_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5175
# EM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
